Pseudo-diff PR1 (seam_fp, nothing applied): mu, c, kappa, lambda measured and logged; the fitted prefill cost in
place of RECOMPUTE_S_PER_TOKEN. Line numbers at HEAD. Everything below runs on the scheduler thread (tick(), the
cache's drain and dispatch, evict_host, cache_finished_req); no lock is added. The prefetcher refuses TP/PP > 1
(next_turn_prefetch.py:468-469), so no rank consensus is involved.

=== new file python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/next_turn_prices.py  (pure policy: no clock, no cache) ===
The prototype agents/seam_fp/proto/next_turn_prices.py, 22 CPU tests passing: DecayedMean, PriceBoard
(observe_admissions / observe_queue / observe_device / observe_eviction; c, mu, kappa, lam, snapshot),
landing_quantile, AdmissionErrorTracker, PrefillCostModel, recompute_wins.

  c(t)      = decayed share (half-life 30 s) of admissions after which no ready turn was left waiting;
              prior 1 (one pseudo-sample), so an idle engine reads 1.
  mu(t)     = 1 + time-weighted decayed mean of ready turns waiting (ready = queued, no storage read of its own
              under way for >= NTP_GPU_BOUND_S = 0.5 s).
  kappa(t)  = c(t) x (parked reads past deadline - own load, "now" reads included) + lam(t) x pending write tokens.
  lam(t)    = decayed mean of the per-pass marginal holding index among host eviction victims, 0 once the last
              eviction is older than 30 s:  index = k x holding_rate(victim),
              k = (c + kappa) x read seconds per token  [seconds of TTFT per token restored by a read],
              holding_rate = sup_{h >= 0.5 s} F(h | idle) / E[min(R, h) | idle]  [per second].
              Units: seconds of TTFT per token-second, the unit of --hicache-storage-next-turn-memory-price.

